Most likely the relative-filename quirk.

Seedance's multipart form requires the filename field to be a relative path, not absolute. Using the full path causes silent failures on some endpoints.

```javascript
// Wrong — causes silent failure
const filename = fullPath  // 'C:\\Users\\Studio\\projects\\scene1.jpg'

// Right
const filename = path.basename(fullPath)  // 'scene1.jpg'
```

Second common cause: race condition between last-frame extraction and upload. Confirm the FFmpeg extraction fully completes and the file exists before the upload call:
```javascript
const stat = fs.statSync(framePath)
if (stat.size === 0) throw new Error('Frame extraction produced empty file')
```
